  "solution": {
    "text": "Ferrocyanide ion <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> is diamagnetic in nature hence <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></math> complex has zero magnetic moment.<br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>Fe</mtext></mrow> </math> atom <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>3d</mtext></mrow> <mtext>6</mtext> </msup> <mtext> </mtext><msup> <mrow> <mtext>4s</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msup> <mtext> </mtext><msup> <mrow> <mtext>4p</mtext></mrow> <mtext>0</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>Fe</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>(II)</mtext></mrow> </math><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>d</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msup> <mtext> </mtext><msup> <mrow> <mtext>sp</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math> hybridisation<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image32-bedc98be-391c-440d-b6f1-3ab35f82f140.jpg\" style=\"width: 328px; height: 77px;\" />",
